Z||000007||Raydar||01-12-2001||10:20 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Tigger:<BR><B>I seen the 2+2 concept at the MI Fiero Show a couple years ago, that was cool.  I'm sure there has to be at least one '89 floating around somewhere.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That may be true, but I suspect that it won't see the light of day for a long time. Probably in some GM exec's garage, or in a warehouse somewhere. <BR>I don't think GM <I>could</I> ever sell it. Since it was never released as a production vehicle, there are probably a bunch of legal (and liability) issues that they'd have to deal with. <BR>Now if they wanted to release <I>body panels</I> through GM parts, that would be a different story.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 01-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||beachbomb||01-12-2001||11:09 AM||||I agree with Raydar, also i was told by the Pontiac rep. that they would never sell these prototypes because they had unproven/untested(safety crap) parts on them that were not releasable to the public yet, or fully tested yet. If someone has this "90 GT", you insanely lucky! I've nerver heard of a '90 being made! I was also told that some '89s may exsist in Exec's garages etc..but all the ones on that Pontiac lot are now recycled <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> I tried like he!! to get the rep. to tell me where one was located or if he knew who had one but i got no-where! But i have no doubt there are a few '89s still around..later..Jim(2 '84 Indys)||||reg||1
Z||000009||loafer87gt||01-12-2001||12:01 PM||||That must be incredibly hard on the designer and engineers to see the product of their passion be scrapped. Perfect examples are the 89 Fiero GT and the Avro Arrow. Both would have been vastly superior to their contemporaries and would have been great for their companies image, yet in the end politics and finances kill the dream before it is realized.||||reg||1
