Z||000013||mrfiero||01-13-2001||05:07 PM||||They didn't have the 3.4 back when that was built.  The Alcan aluminum framed prototyps were running a turbocharged all aluminum 2.9 V-6.  It was conservatively rated at 220 hp and ran circles around almost every other car out there.  If GM had built these they were going to require the owner to attend a  racing school, which would have been included in the purchase price.<P><BR>Unfortunately they never did mass produce these turbo cars (probably too much pressure from the Corvette guys).  The 0-60 times were in the mid to high 5 second range, so it was certainly quick, even by todays standards.  <P>If they had built these Fieros I can guarantee that everyones perception of the Fiero would be much different today.||||reg||10
